        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "chore(ci): enforce changed-file TypeScript LOC ratchet",
        "body": "Closes #106207\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I reviewed the final implementation and validation results.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a repository-maintenance problem where oversized TypeScript files could keep growing because the existing LOC checker was not wired into local checks or CI. A repository-wide fixed baseline also made unrelated pull requests fail whenever legacy oversized files changed elsewhere.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds a baseline-free changed-file ratchet. New production TypeScript files may not exceed 500 physical lines; existing files at or below the limit may not cross it; existing oversized files may stay equal or shrink but may not grow. Test, fixture, mock, generated, deleted, and unrelated legacy files are excluded. The check runs through the normal local/changed-file paths and CI, compares exact event base/head trees, and validates the same GitHub synthetic merge tree when maintainers use the capacity-stall release-gate fallback.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo runtime behavior changes. Contributors get an actionable failure only when their change creates or grows a production TypeScript size violation; unrelated legacy debt no longer blocks their pull request.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxdqv827pjwt28xk9nwct3sy`: final 66 focused LOC/workflow tests, `tsgo:scripts`, formatting, and actionlint/zizmor validation passed. [Actions run](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29250706164)\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxdqpxdvsffbvm1rsp8ynymm`: post-rebase exact-base live LOC check passed and inspected 10 changed production files. [Actions run](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29250561842)\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxdnah0y443mncjc1shq5g1d`: 164 broader focused tests passed across the LOC checker, changed-lane routing, and CI workflow guards. [Actions run](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29247955314)\n- Both edited skill frontmatters parse as YAML.\n- Fresh iterative autoreview: clean after addressing exact-base, untracked-replacement, fast-only routing, and merge-tree execution findings.\n",
